The
use Of mRNA vaccines has transformed our ability to
generate humoral
and cellular responses to vaccination.
While it is appreciated that during infection the production
of cytokines are central to T cell activation and expansion
the basis forthe ability ofthese vaccines to generate patho
gen specific T cell response remain poorly understood. The
studies presented Will identify the
cytokines in these
events and data will be presented that illustrate how this
information can be utilized to enhance and specialize the T
cell responses to infection and cancer
