해외연사 초청 강연
DefiningT cell Subsets
through Cytokine Receptors
'0XIO.65
I60,0 17
in Aging and Disease
Prof Insoo Kang
Yale University School of Medicine
T cells play a critical role in host defense against infections and
nalignancies as well as contribute to the development of inflam-
matory disorders Up on receiving appropriate signals through the
cell receptor, co-stimulatory molecules, and cytokine receptors,
naive T cells become activate proliferate; and differentiate. The
differentiation of effector T cells such as T helper (Th)1 2 and 17
cells; depends on the cytokine milieu. Also, IL7 and IL-15 are es-
sential for the development and maintenance of memory T cells.
Cytokines bind to their cognate receptors expressed on cells; de
livering unique intracellular signals. This raises the possible impli-
cation Of cytokine receptors in defining distinct T
cell subsets.
Indeed, we have identified different subsets of human T cells with
unique functional traits based on the expression cytokine recep
tors
including the IL-7 receptor alpha chain; IL1 receptor 1, and
IL6 receptor alpha chain. During the presentation;
will discuss
the implications of human T cells that differentially express these
pytokine receptors in the context of aging and diseases.
