2021 KF공공외교아카데미 국제워크숍 개최,2021년 05월 25일 16시 40분 25초,,144560,"2021 강원대학교 KF공공외교아카데미 국제워크숍 ＂ 미국의 가치외교와 한국 공공외교에 대한 함의＂ 관심있는 분들의 많은 참여 바랍니다. 다음은 본문 삽입 이미지 대체 텍스트 입니다. 2021 강원대학교 KF 외교아카데미 국제 워크숍 2021 KNU KF Public Diplomacy Academy International Workshop 미국의 가치외교와 한국 공공외교에 대한 함의 The US Value Diplomacy and Its implication for South Korea’s Public Diplomacy 일시: 2021. 06. 17. (목). 10:00-11:30 Date: June 17, 2021 (Thurs). 10:00-11:30 *본 회의는 영-한 동시통역기 제공됩니다. This workshop provides English-Korean simultaneous interpretation KNU강원대학교 정치외교학과, Public Diplomacy Academy, Korea Foundation 한국국제교류재단 The US Value Diplomacy and Its Implication for South Korea’s Public Diplomacy Kangwon National University KF Public Diplomacy Academy Korea Foundation Kangwon National University serves as a KF Public Diplomacy Academy in Gangwon province. It is Supported by the Korea Foundation in its attempt to raise awareness among students of the signficance of publie diplomacy, train public diplomacy specialists, and expand its work across the Gangwon province and beyond. By strengthening publie diplomacy capacity through education and research tailored to specific target audiences, Kangwon National University intends to build the regional diplomatic platform for international understanding and cooperation in East Asia. With such a pioneering effort, Kangwon National University is proud to announce its second public diplomacy workshop. “The US Value Diplomacy and Its Implication for South Korea’s Public Diplomacy” on June 17, 2021 via Zoom. The Choice of focus is motivated by the US Biden Administrations emphasis on value diplomacy, which includes the human rights, democracy, and rule of law. As the great-power competition between the US and China intensifies, two countries are also opposing the values they promote throughout the region of the Indo-Pacific. Against this backdrop, it is necessary to understand their specific infuences on South Korea’s foreign policy and public dipomacy in particular. South Korea’s middle power diplomacy as well as its Peace Regime Initiative toward North Korea, are the topics this workshop intends to concentrated on. Date: June 17th, 2021. (Thursday). 10:00-11:30 AM. (KST) This workshop will be live-streamed via Zoom (ID: 885 3887 4524, PW: 492385) and open to public. Opening Remark (10:00-10:05) Kuyoun Chung (Kangwon National University) Panel (10:05-10:25) Moderator: Woo Jung-yeop (Sejong Institute) Panelist: - Boram Kwon (Korea Institute for Defense Analyses) - Young-joon Kim (Gyeongsang National University) - Wootae Lee (Korea Institute for National Unification) - Andrew Yeo (Catholic University of America) - Xiangfeng Yang (Yonsei University) - Zhang Muui (Pusan National University) Closing Remark (11:25-11:30)",https://wwwk.kangwon.ac.kr/www/selectBbsNttView.do?bbsNo=38&nttNo=144560&&pageUnit=10&searchCtgry=%EC%A0%84%EC%B2%B4%40%40%EC%B6%98%EC%B2%9C&key=279&pageIndex=32,"['https://wwwk.kangwon.ac.kr/www/downloadBbsFile.do?atchmnflNo=63743&bbsNo=38&nttNo=144560&&pageUnit=10&searchCtgry=%EC%A0%84%EC%B2%B4%40%40%EC%B6%98%EC%B2%9C&key=279&pageIndex=32', 'https://wwwk.kangwon.ac.kr/www/downloadBbsFile.do?atchmnflNo=63744&bbsNo=38&nttNo=144560&&pageUnit=10&searchCtgry=%EC%A0%84%EC%B2%B4%40%40%EC%B6%98%EC%B2%9C&key=279&pageIndex=32']",강원대학교,백령광장(춘천),행사안내
