Final Schedule.docx,2019년 11월 26일 11시 42분 30초,법학도서관 201호,134401,"The Future of Public Diplomacy in the midst of Power Competition
Kangwon National University 
KF Public Diplomacy Academy
Korea Foundation
KNU Institute of Social Science Studies 
The Korean Association of Area Studies
Kangwon National University serves as a KF Public Diplomacy Academy in Kangwon Province. It is supported by the Korea Foundation in its attempt to raise awareness among students of the significance of public diplomacy and train public diplomacy specialists. By strengthening public diplomacy capacity through education and research tailored to specific target audiences, Kangwon National University intends to build the regional diplomatic platform for international understanding and cooperation in East Asia.
With such a pioneering effort, Kangwon National University is proud to announce its first Public Diplomacy Workshop, “The Future of Public Diplomacy in the midst of Power Competition,” on November 28, 2019 at Kangwon National University, Chuncheon, Republic of Korea.
The choice of focus is motivated by the following observations. The regional structure has become multipolar with the US-China rivalry and the rise of revisionist states. At the same time, such a rise in multipolarity accompanies the blocization of values. Indeed, as support for the liberal internationalist order has declined, even within the United States, such a trend has enabled other powers to pursue their own values, strengthen their own identities, and project them in various forms of diplomacy. Therefore, the importance of public diplomacy has naturally received more attention these days.
Against such backdrop, this workshop intends to first understand the current security landscape and then discuss the future of public diplomacy in the East Asia region. Experts from the US, China, Japan, Taiwan, Russia, Kazakhstan, and South Korea will discuss their perspectives on the current regional security and normative landscape and their suggestions for public diplomacy to ease such tension in the region.
The Future of Public Diplomacy in the midst of Power Competition
Date: November 28, 2019.
Venue: College of Law (Library)#401, Kangwon National University, Chuncheon.
