발표초록Uncertainty(0831).docx,2015년 08월 21일 08시 00분 00초,,20978,"Uncertainty Analysis of Artificial intelligence Techniques for water quality prediction
ABSTRACT
Although there are many publications on the uncertainty analysis of deterministic water quality models, few have focused on determining the uncertainty of artificial intelligence (AI) techniques, for the prediction of water quality parameters. It is obvious that predictions are not certain, and in the application of results, uncertainty analysis can be more effective. The main reason of uncertainty in AI techniques is their structure and algorithm. They are usually known as data-driven models and their performance is highly dependent on the selected pattern for calibration. Therefore, these models are always sensitive to input data, and the results vary by changing the selected calibration pattern. This fact causes managers to face many problems in making appropriate decisions for monitoring water quality network.  
This presentation is intended to present a pioneering effort in the uncertainty analysis of AI models, i.e. artificial neural network (ANN) and adaptive neuro-fuzzy inference system (ANFIS) techniques. Therefore, the uncertainty analysis of AI techniques (particularly the SVM model) is novel and useful to water quality management. ",https://wwwk.kangwon.ac.kr/www/downloadBbsFile.do?atchmnflNo=15333&bbsNo=38&nttNo=20978&&pageUnit=10&searchCtgry=%EC%A0%84%EC%B2%B4%40%40%EC%B6%98%EC%B2%9C&key=279&pageIndex=105,[],강원대학교,백령광장(춘천),행사안내
