The 11th Northeast Asia 
Management and Economics 
Joint Conference 
(NAMEJC 2013)
INVITATION
 Dear prospective conference participants and honored guests
   We are delighted and honored to invite you all to the 11th Northeast Asia Management and Economics Joint Conference (NAMEJC 2013) with the theme of “Symbiosis and Creation in the Northeast Asia Toward One Asia.” It will be held at Kangwon National University and Hotel Bears in Chuncheon, Korea on November 7-10, 2013.
   To improve and strengthen the academic exchange and economic cooperation in northeast Asia, the National Economics and Management Association of Korea(NEMAK) and the China University Commercial Education Association(CUCEA) had held this kind of international conferences every year in China and Korea alternately since 2002. In commemoration of the historical 11th joint conference, we had planned a very exciting opportunity for scholars, practitioners, policymakers and students to meet and exchange ideas and experiences on several well-chosen topics which can contribute to the advent of the “Age of One Asia” in the near future.
   This year, one key note speech and dozens of papers will be presented at the special working group sessions by scholars or experts from Korea, China and Japan.
   Therefore, we are confident that this year’s conference will provide us with a stimulating environment for the exchange of ideas and prospects on the reality or visibility of “One Asia” to rebuild the governance of the global economy. We are earnestly looking forward to seeing you in Chuncheon and hope that you will enjoy this international conference. 
Sincerely yours,
Hae Young Byun
Professor, Kangwon National University
President, the National Economics and Management Association of Korea
Baocheng Ji(President, Renmin University)
President, CUCEA     
