붙임1-2)공고문(영문).pdf,2013년 09월 04일 08시 00분 00초,,20379,"Information Sheet for 
The 2013 Understanding Korea Essay   Contest
 
 
 
 
The 2013 Understanding Korea Essay Contest
 
The Center for International Affair at AKS is the home of the Understanding Korea 
Project, which seeks to correct inaccurate information on and improve contents about 
Korea in foreign textbooks. We are pleased to announce the 2013 Understanding 
Korea Essay competition, aimed at promoting interest in Korea-related contents in 
foreign textbooks and Understanding Korea materials. Please note the following 
guidelines.
 
1. Themes
  Theme 1: The image of Korea in foreign countries
Subthemes
   i. Thoughts on images of Korea presented in foreign textbooks
    - Reflections on the Korea-related contents you read in textbooks, creative ways 
to improve and increase that contents
   ii. Ways to improve the images of Korea abroad
    - Creative ways to improve the image of Korea in your country
    * Please choose one topic from the two subthemes and write an essay. The essay 
must be written in the application form.
 
  Theme 2: Understanding Korea Materials
Subthemes
   i. Review of the use of Understanding Korea materials
    - How the materials were used, ideas to improve usage
   ii. Ideas for developing Understanding Korea materials
    - Strong and weak points of the materials, additions, and revisions
    - Ideas and topics for Understanding Korea materials, a detailed plan or proposal 
to develop material
    * Please choose one topic from the two subthemes and write an essay. The essay 
must be written in the application form.
Title
Winner
Prizes
