  ※ The Understanding Korea materials are those distributed by the Center for 
International Affairs at AKS. Full details for the materials can be found on the 
homepage of the Center: (http://www.ikorea.ac.kr/)
 
2. Eligibility
  Everyone interested in the Understanding Korea Project
 
3. Submission
    - All essays must be written in the essay contest application (downloaded from 
the Center's homepage) and submitted via email to highspirit@aks.ac.kr
    - All other submissions will be disqualified.
    - Submitted essays will not be returned and the Center for International Affairs 
will obtain copyright.
    - Applicants can apply to both themes and different subthemes separately. In 
other words, if they wish to do so, applicants can submit four essays for all 
four subthemes.
 
4. Language of Essay: Korean or English
5. Deadline: September 1 (Sun) -- September 30 (Mon), 2013, 6:00 pm (Korean time)
            Submissions after the deadline will not be accepted.
 
6. Prizes
  ※ Taxes related to the acceptance of and use of the prize are the winners’ 
responsibility.
  ※ All applicants will received a souvenir (First 400 applicants only)
 
7.  Announcement: Friday, November 8, 2013
The result of the contest will be posted on the Center's homepage
(http://intl.ikorea.ac.kr/korean)and all winners will be notified individually.
 
