Day 1
1. Short intro talk - What is biochar, how is it used, and how is it made
2. Demo Fabrication of 200 L TLUD natural draft biochar oven (UB J-RO)
a. A new [expensive] or good condition used [cheap to free] metal 200l barrel. An
open top barrel with a clamp on lid (clamp not necessary) is best. The metal
barrels with a sealed lid and one or two threaded openings can also be used but
they need to be cut open. This is not difficult, but if they contained hydrocarbons
or other flammable liquids or unknown liquids they might explode if not handled
properly, even if they appear to be empty. For safety’s sake they should be cut
open smoothly about 2-3 cm below the rim by a professional that knows how to
take proper precautions.
b. A hand held side grinder & 2 thin aluminum oxide blades.
c. A strong drill with good ¼” & ½” metal drilling bits.
d. Two meters of 1 to 2 mm non-stretching cord.
e. Two 65 cm lengths of 4 to 5 cm angle iron or similar bars to lay across the top of
the feedstock chamber to create a 2.5 to 4 cm gap between lip and lid.
f. A 1 m x 1 m sheet of metal, flexible enough to be bent into a smoke stack of 25
to 30 cm diameter.
g. 10 sets of ¼” by ½” long nut, bolt and lock washer.
h. A good ‘straight edge’ (ruler like) at least 60 cm long.
i. A tape measure.
j. Eye protection.
