Suwyoung_Ly.hwp,2011년 04월 01일 08시 00분 00초,,19702,"␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Assay of biological  neuro signal in the brain of a primate and interface technology
Catecholamine, dopamine, and epinephrine are known as the neurotransmitters responsible for human cognition and behavior. They are involved in the entire neuro cognitive system, managing all kinds of activities, thoughts, and decisions. In addition, these chemicals control memory, muscular motion, body balance, emotional stimulation and depression, secretion of hormones, neuropsychiatric disorders, and epilepsy. Diagnosis through the minute detection of these compounds in our body is very important for a variety of technological applications in many fields such as mind-computer interface technology, control of memory, excitation, mental diseases, stress prevention and body development, treatment of endocrine diseases, and remote control of equipment. Nonetheless, the concentration of these chemicals is usually less than 1 mg/L; thus making a real time detection of them extremely difficult. In addition, various biochemical substances in our body, the flow of charged materials, and fluctuating electromagnetic waves hamper the detection. To date, there has been no published study, nationally or internationally, on internal, real time diagnosis and analysis of such neurotransmitters. As such, our laboratory has published a number of studies on the following areas: Diagnosis, Sensors, Neuro signal, Recognition, Investigation, Spectro photometry
  

