Abstract 
  
Title: 
Small 
molecule 
drug 
discovery 
targeting DGAT1 for the treatment of 
metabolic disorders 
 
Abstract: Obesity and type II diabetes are 
intrinsically 
linked 
and 
considered 
as 
pandemic life-threatening diseases. DGAT1 
is a key enzyme for lipid metabolism.  The 
phenotype of DGAT1 knock-out mice 
validates DGAT1 as an intriguing target for 
the drug discovery in metabolic disease 
area.  Multiple chemotypes were pursued 
to identify potent and efficacious DGAT1 
inhibitors and that yielded some exciting 
chemistry discoveries.  Important lessons 
were learned that would potentially impact 
future drug discovery programs.",https://wwwk.kangwon.ac.kr/www/downloadBbsFile.do?atchmnflNo=14595&bbsNo=38&nttNo=19575&&pageUnit=10&searchCtgry=%EC%A0%84%EC%B2%B4%40%40%EC%B6%98%EC%B2%9C&key=279&pageIndex=239,[],강원대학교,백령광장(춘천),행사안내
